    "notes": "Five parts: Soprano, Alto, Tenor, Bass (closed score: S+A share the treble staff, T+B the bass staff, bracketed; each shared staff MUST be split into two parts by stem direction) and Piano (braced grand staff, ONE part, never split - its right hand has two voices in the verse, which must stay inside the piano part). Systems 1 (introduction) and 4 (interlude) show only the piano: the choir parts have invisible whole-measure rests there. The verse (mm. 15-23) is repeated: verse 1 and verse 2 are stacked; m.22 = 1st ending (verse 1 \"ny wings\"), m.23 = 2nd ending (verse 2 \"the sky\"). Segno m.5, To Coda after m.10, D.S. al Coda after m.23, Coda m.24 - notated order, not unrolled. Lyrics are under both choir staves; truth attaches them to Soprano and Tenor (Alto/Bass sing the same syllables on the same rhythm)."
  },
